In article <4984@aplcen.apl.jhu.edu> theune@aplcen.apl.jhu.edu (Peter Theune) writes:
>I think you've been whammied by the dreaded "sticky cursed" item.  I
>don't have the source code here, but if I remember correctly, some items
>are "sticky cursed" which means that you have to get rid of them as soon
>as you uncurse them, or they will be cursed again. I think this also
>applys to items you remove and place in your pack.... 

Loadstones are supposed to behave as described.  It's a feature, and was
deliberately programmed in.

"Sticky cursed" is just an old name for cursed, prominently appearing in one
spoiler sheet and referring to ordinary curses on items which cannot be
removed or unwielded (rings, armor, weapons, amulets).  If such an item is
removed by a nymph, it's still cursed, but if you uncurse it it's uncursed for
good.  Loadstones are the only items which become cursed again when dropped.
Your pack has nothing to do with it; objects never become cursed just by being
placed in your pack.
